{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For the given function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases by <math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> for every increase of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["44"], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math>. For a function defined by an equation of the form <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> are positive constants, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"r percent sign\"><mi>r</mi><mo>%</mo></math> for every increase of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>. The given equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction 2 x Over 6 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis left parenthesis 1.2 right parenthesis squared right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 6 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><msup><mfenced><mn>1.2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.44 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 6 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.44</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 44 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 6 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>44</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. This equation is of the form <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"a equals 27\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>27</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"r equals 44\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>r</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>44</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"k equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>k</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It follows that the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"44 percent sign\"><mn>44</mn><mo>%</mo></math> for every increase of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.&nbsp;Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Alternate approach: It's given that <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. An increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> can be represented by the expression <math alttext=\"x plus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The value of <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> can be found by&nbsp;substituting <math alttext=\"x plus 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, which yields <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x plus 6 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. By the product property of exponents, this equation is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction Baseline dot left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript six thirds\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction Baseline dot left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis squared\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which can be rewritten as&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction Baseline dot left parenthesis 1.44 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mn>1.44</mn></mfenced></math>. Since <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 27 left parenthesis 1.20 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.20</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, it follows that <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis dot left parenthesis 1.44 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1.44</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, for any value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is <math alttext=\"1.44\"><mn>1.44</mn>\n</math> times, or <math alttext=\"44 percent sign\"><mn>44</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than, the value of <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. It's given that the value of <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> for every increase in the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> by <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. It follows that the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math>.</p>", "externalid": "e5403cac-ceb7-4643-b03d-c3f63fe73713", "correct_answer": ["44"]}